build/
# `poetry build` output at the repo root. Not ignored until now, so a build left a
# multi-megabyte untracked wheel in the tree, one `git add -A` away from being committed.
# Deliberately NOT `src/*/dist/`: src/robovast_nav/dist/ holds wheels that are *tracked*
# (robovast_nav 1.0.0, committed at some point and now stale), and a rule claiming to
# ignore tracked files misleads without changing anything.
/dist/
# The sibling distributions' build output. `src/robovast_nav/dist/` once held *tracked*
# wheels (robovast_nav 1.0.0, committed in an early cluster commit and stale ever since
# against the package's 2.0.0); they are gone, so the glob is honest now.
src/*/dist/
install/
log/
**/__pycache__
venv
.venv
.vscode/
**/.cache
**/.robovast_*
/results
frontend/ui/node_modules
frontend/ui/dist
# TypeScript's incremental-build caches: machine-specific, and rewritten by every
# `npm run build`, so committing them meant a dirty tree after any UI build.
**/*.tsbuildinfo
# Node build deps for any package-shipped web bundle (e.g. src/robovast_nav/web,
# the run-view panel remotes). Their built output lands elsewhere as package data.
**/node_modules
# Built Module-Federation panel bundle (package data). Generated by the web/ project's
# `npm run build`; the wheel build must run it (like frontend/ui/dist), so it is not committed.
src/robovast_nav/robovast_nav/web/dist
# @module-federation/vite's build-time scratch dir (diagnostics), written next to the sources.
**/.mf
.env
# Staged copy of frontend/ui/dist for the wheel (see `make ui-stage`).
src/robovast/_ui/
